{
  "about" : "Paztport intent conformance vectors (spec intent.md): how an item reads, and what the checks P1 and P2 answer for the items a service is handed under `intent`. Every answer is written by hand from the spec. `items` gives an `item` as the text a block carries, and its `facts`: each fact name to the JCS text of its value as a JSON string, so the integer 100 is \"100\" and the string x is \"\\\"x\\\"\", or null when the item does not read as an intent item, whether the wire reader refuses its text or its schema does. `requests` gives, for a service that handles a request, whether the hand-over is `verified` and whether the service acts on `intent` (`actsOn`); when it does, `stamps` lists each stamp of the chain in order with its signer `svc` and the `items` its block holds under `intent`, null when the block does not name it and [] when it names it with none, and when it does not, `stamps` is null and nothing is handed over. Each item in `stamps` is wire-valid JSON, so a block can hold it. `needs` is the names of the facts the handler requires. `read` is the answer of check P1 over the items, `OK` or `INTENT_MISMATCH`, and `unreadSigner` the signer of the block holding items that do not read, null when they read. `require` is the answer of check P2 for `needs`: `OK`, `INTENT_MISSING` or `INTENT_MISMATCH`, the last when the items of a verified hand-over do not read. Cases may be added; a recorded answer changes only with a protocol change.",
